    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9271" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνοργίαστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not celebrated with orgies,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					898
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τελεταί,</span> i.e. <i>no
			true</i> mysteries, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.156
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of a god or
			person <i>in whose honour no orgies are held,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Epin.</u>
				985d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>uninitiated,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.268
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμύητος καὶ ἀ. τῶν ἱερῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Them.
					<u>Or.</u>
					13.166c
				</span></i>
			.</div>
